  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 310 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nLow amplitude ridging will remain in place at the beginning of the \nmid-range period. With deep troughing over the Hudson Bay, a strong \nnorthern stream jet will stretch from the Canadian Rockies through \nthe Great Lakes. Longwave troughing will eventually contribute to \nridge breakdown Friday/Saturday, though mild temperatures will \npersist. NBM highlights fairly high confidence in continued \nanomalous warmth with inner-quartile ranges decreasing from 5F on \nThursday to 2F by Friday and 4F for Saturday. This suggests a low \nvariation in potential outcomes highlighted by NWP guidance thus the \nhigher confidence. Though height falls will overspread the area this \nweekend as southwesterly flow becomes reestablished, precipitation \nprospects remain fairly poor through the weekend. This is because \nthe aforementioned longwave will continue to dig south along the \nWest Coast with a deep cutoff low taking shape by Sunday/Monday. \nThis cutoff will then stall with shortwave ridging then building \nacross the Central and Southerns Plains. The result will be warmer \nweather lingering a bit longer into the mid-range forecast. \nPrecipitation probabilities continue to slowly trend down as upper-\nlevel dynamics largely miss the area to the northwest. This limits \nPoPs to around 30% or less, focused across the Sandhills up towards \nthe Pine Ridge through Monday. Confidence for Monday and beyond \nremains quite low as evolution of the upper-level low is fairly \nuncertain. Deterministic solutions from the ECMWF/GFS both lift it \nnorth and east, crossing the Central Rockies sometime \nWednesday/Thursday. While moisture should increase in the lead-up to \narrival of this disturbance, ensembles paint fairly modest \nprecipitable water values in the lead up to stronger synoptic lift. \nThis may hinder precipitation efficiency and subsequently, amounts. \nEPS/GEFS probabilities are noisy though the majority (90% of \nmembers) show at least measurable rain around the middle of the \nweek. Day-to-day predictability will likely remain poor until at \nleast the upcoming weekend so continue to check with later forecasts \nfor details.",
